# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-repo-concurrency  (artifact-keeper#5243, for 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-files (the oracle writes N Maven
# jars to the mock). LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts come from the backend image's bundled
# Grype; the oracle recreates the backend once with the
# scan-queue-upload-image-rescan tier's grype stub in front of it
# (fixtures/grype-stub.yml there), so every scan takes a known extra time.
#
# THE CHANGE
# #5243  Scans share MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_EXTRACTIONS permits (default 4), with
#        a per-repository fair share (default 2) layered in front (#2555). A
#        repository alone may use all 4, but a scan waiting over its fair share
#        only woke when one of the repository's own fair-share scans finished,
#        so after the first wave a lone repository ran 2 scans at a time and
#        the 2 permits its first-wave bursts returned stayed idle.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on main before the fix, GREEN on the fix:
#              N=12 concurrent first pulls of distinct clean jars through one
#              fail_closed scan_on_proxy Maven Remote. The oracle samples the
#              stubbed grype processes in the backend every 0.5 s; once the
#              first wave of 4 has finished, 4 scans must run at once again
#              (main: never more than 2). MEASURE prints the wall time of the
#              whole fill and the mean scans running per sample.
#   (CONTROL)  both images: every pull is 200 X-AK-Scan: clean with the
#              upstream's bytes, and the first wave runs 4 at once.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: 12 pulls at once, plus setup calls.
COVERS="5243"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
